F=[
('F01','HIGH','Any app on the paired phone can supply accepted credit-like notifications','apps/android-observer-app/app/src/main/java/com/youpi/observer/PaymentNotificationListenerService.java:30; apps/payment-api/src/routes/pollers.routes.js:348',
 'The Java listener signs and forwards matching incoming-credit text. It does not check the originating app package/signing identity.',
 'A signed payload labelled with a test non-bank package and an unused synthetic UTR changed an isolated matching order to SUCCESS. This reproduces the server gap; an actual malicious Android APK was not installed. Pairing authenticates the phone, not the bank.',
 'Bind permitted source packages and signing identities per receiving account; preserve and verify that provenance in the signed payload. Keep notification acceptance explicitly labelled as a platform policy. Genuine bank verification still requires independent bank/provider evidence.',
 'An untrusted local app on the receiving phone can cause an unpaid order to look Paid and trigger game-wallet credit.'),
('F02','HIGH','Native notification title is lost during server parsing','apps/payment-api/src/routes/pollers.routes.js:325; apps/android-observer-app/app/src/main/java/com/youpi/observer/ApiClient.java:169',
 'Native extraction reads title plus text and sends both inside rawNotification. The paired server path reparses rawNotification.text alone.',
 'A native-shaped payload with amount/received in the title and UTR in the text returned HTTP 200 NON_PAYMENT_ALERT. The matching order remained ACTIVE even though the native payload also supplied parsed amount/reference.',
 'Normalize title and text together before the trusted server parser, with a bounded combined length. Test actual Slice/GPay/PhonePe notification formats and duplicate expanded/collapsed notifications.',
 'Valid receiving notifications can be silently acknowledged and removed from the phone queue without marking the order Paid.'),
('F03','HIGH','SUCCESS can commit without a callback outbox record','apps/payment-api/src/services/receiving-mirror.js:78; packages/core/src/webhook-engine.js:45',
 'enqueue returns an empty delivery ID when the merchant URL is missing or rejected. The mirror does not treat this return value as a reservation failure.',
 'Removing the callback URL after setup, then accepting an alert, produced SUCCESS and a ledger entry with zero webhook_deliveries rows. Restoring the URL later has no row to retry.',
 'Persist a durable pending callback event even when the endpoint is temporarily unconfigured, or reject/pause acceptance until a callback reservation can be made. Alert operators and preserve an explicit replay path.',
 'The game never receives its success event although the customer has paid and the portal shows Paid.'),
('F04','HIGH','A one-to-two-minute-late alert can miss the pending order','apps/payment-api/src/services/receiving-mirror.js:51; packages/core/src/timing-engine.js:156',
 'Processing timeout moves an order to VERIFICATION_PENDING, but mirror eligibility still cuts off at processing_expires_at.',
 'An alert observed two minutes after order creation, after its 30-second processing window, returned UNMATCHED while the order stayed VERIFICATION_PENDING. The ten-minute creation cap does not extend the earlier processing expiry.',
 'Define a safe late-confirmation window and correlate by a real order-bound reference or authoritative evidence. Do not simply relax the amount/time match when the same UPI can have a new same-amount order.',
 'A valid late bank/app notification will not generate the immediate SUCCESS callback the product promises for delayed payments.'),
('F05','HIGH','Webhook destination checks do not validate resolved IP addresses','packages/common/src/secrets.js:180; packages/core/src/webhook-engine.js:134',
 'The URL guard blocks private literal IPs and a few private hostname suffixes. Callback delivery uses ordinary fetch DNS resolution.',
 'With private-webhook permission disabled, http://127.0.0.1.nip.io/callback was accepted, and DNS resolved that hostname to 127.0.0.1. This probe confirmed hostname validation plus resolution; it did not send an exploit request into production.',
 'Use a shared outbound HTTP client that checks every resolved address and pins the validated destination through connection establishment, for webhook and integration requests. Continue refusing redirects and private/reserved networks.',
 'A merchant-controlled DNS name can route callback requests into local/private services: server-side request forgery.'),
('F06','HIGH','Refund Idempotency-Key does not prevent a second refund','apps/payment-api/src/platform/payments.js:193; apps/payment-api/src/routes/refunds.routes.js:61',
 'The scoped refund wrapper requires Idempotency-Key but does not bind it to a refund request. Without body.refundId, the delegated route generates a new random refund ID each time.',
 'Two identical authenticated /v1/refunds requests with the same Idempotency-Key and amount created two refund rows and called the simulated provider twice. Both fit within the remaining original balance, so the cumulative reservation guard did not prevent the duplicate intention.',
 'Atomically bind merchant plus idempotency key to a canonical refund fingerprint and stable refund ID; reject changed requests and return the original result for a retry. Test timeout, duplicate and partial-refund cases through /v1/refunds.',
 'A normal merchant network retry can refund a customer twice, up to the remaining refundable amount.'),
('F07','MEDIUM','Legacy collection still has a hard INR 100 minimum','apps/payment-api/src/routes/dynamopay.routes.js:191',
 'The preferred /v1/payments accepts positive paise under saved rules. The still-supported /v1.0/collect/upi route has an additional hard minimum.',
 'A legacy request for INR 1 was rejected INVALID_AMOUNT even with channel minimum saved as 0. This contradicts the requested zero configurable floor across integrations.',
 'Reuse the canonical positive-paise and saved-channel validation in the legacy adapter; add a below-INR-100 legacy regression case.',
 'Customers using the legacy SDK/API cannot accept the same small payments that the preferred API allows.'),
('F08','MEDIUM','New merchant legacy credentials fail until server restart','apps/payment-api/src/routes/dynamopay.routes.js:91',
 'Legacy merchant credentials are loaded into a process-local map only when routes are registered.',
 'A merchant created after registration received HTTP 401 from the legacy wallet endpoint even with correctly derived legacy credentials. The scoped dp_live API uses the database and is not this cache.',
 'Resolve the current merchant and derived credential on demand, or refresh/invalidate the legacy cache when onboarding changes it. Test onboarding then immediate legacy API use without restarting.',
 'An onboarded customer can receive valid legacy details that do not work until the service is restarted.'),
('F09','MEDIUM','Legacy wallet omits notification-confirmed funds','apps/payment-api/src/routes/dynamopay.routes.js:145; packages/db/src/repositories/ledger.repository.js:21',
 'Notification collections correctly post into NOTIFICATION_CLEARING. The legacy wallet unsettled projection only reads PROVIDER_CLEARING.',
 'After an isolated INR 100 notification-confirmed payment, NOTIFICATION_CLEARING held 10,000 paise while /v1.0/wallet returned unsettledbalance 0.00 and no separate notification-clearing field.',
 'Expose notification-clearing funds as a separately named accounting balance and reconcile it to actual bank credit. Do not label it settled bank cash.',
 'The customer sees successful deposits but incomplete recorded balance information and may reconcile against the wrong total.')]

