overview=[('What this repo does','Dynamo Pay creates merchant payment orders, presents hosted UPI checkout, accepts configured provider or notification evidence, posts ledger records and sends signed merchant callbacks. The assumed workload is multiple independent gaming-site merchants with concurrent players on a shared platform. The current one-active-slot-per-receiving-account allocator and single hosted Free instance constrain that workload.'),('Verdict',summary),('Baseline',f'Prepared {now}. Local HEAD and fetched GitHub main: {rev}. Render current live commit matches. All audit probes used isolated data. No credentials were rotated, no production policies were enabled, no live money was transferred, and no existing financial records were reset.'),('Skills and review stages','Ponytail, Ponytail Audit and Render Monitor were used. No separate Developer, Tester or UAT skill was available in the session or found in the local skill catalog. Developer review, automated testing and a UAT matrix were performed directly. The PDF skill was used to render and inspect this report.'),('Coverage honesty',f'{len(inventory)} tracked source/config/test files were read by the inventory scanner. Critical paths were traced, with section-level review in {sum(r[0] in deep for r in inventory)} files; executed suites and review depth are recorded per file in the CSV. Inventory reading, syntax checks and green tests are not semantic sign-off for every line. Legacy TypeScript and auxiliary/demo paths are not all active production code. Runtime code was not changed by this audit.')]
production=[('Live service',f'{host["service"]}, region {host["region"]}, plan {host["plan"]}, deploy status {host["deployStatus"]}, branch {host["branch"]}, auto-deploy trigger {host["autoDeployTrigger"]}. Public origin https://dynamo-pay.onrender.com. Local, remote and live source agree at {rev[:7]}.'),('Database',f'PostgreSQL status {host["postgresStatus"]}, plan {host["postgresPlan"]}. Current expiry returned by Render: {host["postgresExpiresAt"]}. Arrange migration/renewal before 30 November 2026; no plan change was made. Always-on service, backup/restore evidence and recovery objectives are outstanding.'),('Current configuration',f'Read-only aggregate snapshot: {db["merchants"]} merchant record, states {db["merchantStates"]}; {db["pp_api_keys"]} scoped API keys; {db["provider_connections"]} provider connections; {db["android_devices"]} Android devices; {db["pp_receiver_devices"]} bound phones; {db["activeNotificationPolicies"]} enabled notification policies; {db["payment_sessions"]} payment sessions and {db["webhook_deliveries"]} callback records. This is not a completed customer installation. Legacy derived credentials are separate from the zero scoped-key count. No inbox credential values were requested or disclosed.'),('Live HTTP smoke','; '.join(x['path']+' = '+str(x['status']) for x in live['checks'])+'. Anonymous protected APIs correctly return 401. Readiness/portal responses show liveness only. APK 503 blocks current public observer installation. No full authenticated customer payment was executed on production.'),('Observability limits','The Render connector previously required reauthentication and CLI was unavailable; existing saved API access in the user-confirmed Nitish workspace supplied service/deploy/database metadata. Historical runtime logs and cloud CPU/memory/HTTP latency metrics were not certified in this pass. Browser inventory returned no usable browser and native pipe unavailable; visual UAT cannot be passed.')]
evidence=[('Regression',f'{reg["passedSuites"]}/{reg["suiteCount"]} suites, {reg["totalTests"]} reported tests, {reg["durationSeconds"]} seconds; testedAt {reg["testedAt"]}. Some service-dependent acceptance tests may be skipped. The curated runner omits tracked suites: '+(', '.join(unrun) if unrun else 'none')+'. Both were executed separately: two tests passed, including PostgreSQL cleanup against its dedicated synthetic schema. The pre-existing untracked e2e-upi-flow.test.js was not promoted into the official run.'),('Static checks','Typecheck exit 0. Runtime build exit 0: 214 JavaScript runtime/tool files validated (including the untracked benchmark script present locally). Tracked-source secret-pattern scan passed for 571 paths; this is not a full Git-history credential audit.'),('Dependencies','npm audit --omit=dev reported '+str(deps['metadata']['vulnerabilities']['total'])+' known production dependency advisories at scan time. A zero advisory count does not certify authentication, financial logic or unknown supply-chain vulnerabilities.'),('PostgreSQL integration','New separate temporary-schema test passed notification SUCCESS, clearing ledger, outbox, source label, duplicate idempotency, atomic rollback and retry after rollback. Connection search_path was set before adapter construction; public customer rows were untouched and the schema was dropped. These checks are real PostgreSQL queries, not provider/phone acceptance.'),('Diagnostic probes','Seven isolated diagnostic tests reproduced nine gaps F01-F09. Evidence is in production-audit-probes-2026-11-01.json and the executable diagnostic script. Its assertions deliberately verify existing defects; it is not part of the curated passing production regression suite.'),('Performance','Earlier 50-sample local on-disk SQLite/HTTP benchmark: alert-to-callback p50 '+str(bench['summaryMs']['alertToCallbackReceivedMs']['p50'])+' ms, p95 '+str(bench['summaryMs']['alertToCallbackReceivedMs']['p95'])+' ms; wallet p95 '+str(bench['summaryMs']['alertToWalletCommittedMs']['p95'])+' ms. Automatic retry after initial 503 completed in '+str(round(bench['retry']['alertToWalletCommittedMs']/1000,2))+' seconds. No real bank, Android app, hosted payment latency or customer backend was included.')]
gates=[('Fix order','First repair F06 refund idempotency and F05 DNS-safe egress; lock down F01 source provenance before using notification-based game-wallet credit. Then repair F02 title/body normalization, F03 callback reservation and F04 late-confirmation design. Resolve F07-F09 before supporting legacy integrations.'),('Release verification','Turn the reproduced cases into normal regression tests expecting the corrected behavior. Run typecheck, runtime build, secret/dependency checks, the 56-suite regression and the isolated PostgreSQL acceptance again. Review exact commit/CI/deployment; do not treat these still-failing behaviors as approved merely because the old tests pass.'),('Infrastructure','Choose always-on hosting with measured capacity and an appropriate database retention plan. Set monitoring, external error alerts, backup/restore procedure and recovery ownership. One active receiving slot, shared-UPI amount collisions and sequential callback-retry backlog must be covered by a load/capacity plan.'),('Customer acceptance','Complete all UAT rows, including signed current APK on Vivo, trusted bank/payment app capture, real small credit and bank statement match, customer raw-signature verification and durable wallet credit once, callback failure/recovery, revoked/offline phone and late alerts. Confirm provider/bank acceptance separately for refunds, payouts and external collections.'),('Callback timing limits','Immediate callback attempt happens after accepted evidence commits. Default background callback sweep is 5 seconds, each HTTP attempt timeout 10 seconds, total default attempts 5. Retry delays used are 5 seconds, 30 seconds, 2 minutes and 10 minutes. The retry loop awaits rows sequentially; 20 unresponsive endpoints can occupy a sweep for roughly 200 seconds, although online alert-specific immediate attempts are separate. This is a code-derived worst-case scenario, not a measured hosted load test.'),('Final sign-off','Verdict: NOT READY. A controlled non-money demonstration can show the mechanics, but unrestricted customer collections and an instant-callback SLA are not justified by current evidence. Not checked: every historical line/dependency manually, native compilation/device, genuine bank/provider flows, customer game-wallet integration, browser visual UAT, hosted high-load/recovery tests and production CPU/memory/log metrics. No automatic repair, commit, merge or deployment was performed in this audit.')]

